  <page_number>227</page_number>
  <running_head>Lib.6. De politeia sub Abraham</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>Atq</catchword>
    <signature>Pa</signature>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">
      <i>Communis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="2">
      <i>est, qua figurabatur quae ad foedus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="3">
      <i>utrunq; operum &amp; fidei pertinent.</i>Gal.3.24.</l>
    <l n="4" para="true">Huius umbrae cum corpore suo sunt duo membra</l>
    <l n="5" type="diagram" level="1">Primum, Abrahamū ex Agare ancilla</l>
    <l n="6" type="diagram" level="1">serua secundū carné filium ad ser-</l>
    <l n="7" type="diagram" level="1">uitute, qui eijcitur ne sit haeres cū</l>
    <l n="8" type="diagram" level="1">altero filio, suscepisse.</l>
    <l n="9" type="diagram" level="1">Secundū, Abrahamū ex uxore libera</l>
    <l n="10" type="diagram" level="1">per promissionem gratuitam nul-</l>
    <l n="11" type="diagram" level="1">la sua vi, sed secundum spiritum</l>
    <l n="12" type="diagram" level="1">Isacum progenuisse, qui etsi ab</l>
    <l n="13" type="diagram" level="1">Ismaele filio serue profequeba-</l>
    <l n="14" type="diagram" level="1">tur, ipso tamen eiecto haereditate</l>
    <l n="15" type="diagram" level="1">potitus est.</l>
    <l n="16" type="diagram" level="1">label: bra</l>
    <l n="17" type="diagram" level="1">Sina quae extra terram promissio-</l>
    <l n="18" type="diagram" level="1">nis in Arabia sita, qualis est eti-</l>
    <l n="19" type="diagram" level="1">am Ierusalem, quae liberos gignit</l>
    <l n="20" type="diagram" level="1">seruos, qui ex foederis operum for-</l>
    <l n="21" type="diagram" level="1">mula solum, vel alteri adiunctum</l>
    <l n="22" type="diagram" level="1">volunt iustificari, &amp; proinde eijci-</l>
    <l n="23" type="diagram" level="1">untur ab haereditate, quam nun-</l>
    <l n="24" type="diagram" level="1">quam obtinebunt.</l>
    <l n="25" type="diagram" level="1">label: Membra sunt</l>
    <l n="26" type="diagram" level="2">Foedus gratuitum, qualis est illa caele-</l>
    <l n="27" type="diagram" level="2">stis Ierusolyma, quae filios promis-</l>
    <l n="28" type="diagram" level="2">sione gratuita, sola fide apprehens-</l>
    <l n="29" type="diagram" level="2">a ad salutem secundum spiritum</l>
    <l n="30" type="diagram" level="2">gignit: qui eiectis caeteris qui ipsos</l>
    <l n="31" type="diagram" level="2">profequuntur, haereditatem poss-</l>
    <l n="32" type="diagram" level="2">idebant.</l>
  </main_text>
  <marginalia>
    <note side="right" at="Primum, Abrahamū ex" line_from="5" line_to="5">Gal.3.22. 23.</note>
  </marginalia>
  <notes>The brace diagram is printed in the body; labels "bra" and "Membra sunt" stand beside the braces. The first brace group's "Gal. 3.22. 23." is a marginal reference at right. The catchword "Atq" and signature "Pa" at the foot are uncertain.</notes>
